Third-party material

The files wasm/cspice.wasm and wasm/cspice.mjs are compiled from the CSPICE
toolkit, version N0066, which is produced by the Navigation and Ancillary
Information Facility (NAIF) at the Jet Propulsion Laboratory, California
Institute of Technology, under contract with NASA. The build downloads NAIF's
N0066 package from the NAIF server, verifies it against a pinned SHA-256, and
applies the four patches in patches/ (function return types and one include that
WebAssembly needs); each patched file states in its header that it is modified.
docs/cspice-source-provenance.md gives the details, and a CI check fails if the
compiled source differs from NAIF's in any other way. The artifacts currently
committed were compiled from the arturania/cspice fork
(https://github.com/arturania/cspice), from which the patches originate; CI
builds both ways with one compiler and finds the resulting cspice.wasm identical
byte for byte.

CSPICE is distributed under NAIF's own terms, not under the Apache License; see
https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/naif/rules.html before redistributing. Modified code is
not supported by NAIF. To obtain the SPICE Toolkit itself, its documentation, and
kernels, go to https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/naif/toolkit.html.

The file wasm/cspice.wasi.wasm is compiled from the same NAIF N0066 package with
the same patches by scripts/build-cspice-wasi.sh, for WASI 0.1 and the WebAssembly MVP.
It statically links wasi-libc (https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-libc, at the commit
pinned in that script; multi-licensed under the Apache License 2.0 with LLVM
exceptions, the Apache License 2.0, and the MIT License, with portions from musl
under MIT, cloudlibc under BSD-2-Clause, and dlmalloc under CC0) and the LLVM
compiler-rt builtins (Apache License 2.0 with LLVM exceptions).

The file bench/spacewasm-host/src/wasi.rs is adapted from the WASI bindings in
SpaceWasm (https://github.com/nasa/SpaceWasm, crates/spacewasm_tools, v0.8.0-rc.3,
Copyright 2026 California Institute of Technology, Apache License 2.0), which derive
in part from wasmtime's wasi-common crate (Apache License 2.0 with LLVM exception).
The harness in bench/spacewasm-host links the spacewasm, wasi-common, and wiggle
crates at build time; none of them is redistributed here.

The kernel fixtures under test/fixtures are bounded subsets of, or copies of,
public NAIF and PDS kernels (leapseconds, planetary constants, a de440s subset,
Cassini reconstructed ephemeris and instrument kernels, and the New Horizons MU69
low-polygon shape model), included only to make the tests deterministic.

